# Std — Order

`std/order.ssc` shipped with zero coverage and was broken on every lane — three independent
defects (`v2/BUGS.md` `anonymous-given-instance-unresolvable-by-summon-or-using`, and the module's
own header note). This exercises every exported helper over `Int`/`Double`/`String`.

`Boolean` is exercised via the named instance (`orderBoolean.compare`) directly rather than through
the generic `compare`/`min`/`max` helpers: those helpers, called with `Order[Boolean]` in scope
alongside `Order[Int]`/`Order[Double]`/`Order[String]`, hit a separate, still-open reference-front
defect — `v2/BUGS.md` `generic-using-resolution-miscompiles-for-a-later-instance`.

[Order, orderBoolean, compare, lt, gt, lte, gte, min, max](std/order.ssc)

```scalascript
println(compare(3, 5))
println(compare(5, 3))
println(compare(5, 5))
println(lt(3, 5))
println(gt(3, 5))
println(lte(5, 5))
println(gte(5, 5))
println(min(3, 5))
println(max(3, 5))

println(compare(3.0, 2.0))
println(min(3.0, 2.0))

println(compare("apple", "banana"))
println(min("apple", "banana"))
println(max("apple", "banana"))

println(orderBoolean.compare(false, true))
println(orderBoolean.compare(true, false))
println(orderBoolean.compare(true, true))
```
